{%- liquid
  assign number_of_products = section.settings.related_count

  if recommendations.products and recommendations.products_count > 0
    assign related_collection = recommendations
  endif

  assign complementary_products = product.metafields.shopify--discovery--product_recommendation.complementary_products.value
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  This used to be wrapped in Shopify's stock <product-recommendations>
  custom element, which fetches this same section again via
  routes.product_recommendations_url and swaps its own JS-managed
  placeholder once/if that fetch resolves. That JS-driven layer is
  gone now — after two rounds of chasing an "invisible element still
  reserving space" bug inside it (most recently a hidden
  product-grid-item under .visually-invisible, which is only
  opacity:0 and never actually left layout), plain server-rendered
  Liquid is more reliable here and the fallback below already covers
  what that fetch was for anyway: recommendations.products is already
  populated directly on this render when Shopify has real ones for
  this product, with no extra fetch required, and the fallback covers
  every case where it doesn't.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="pm-homepage pm-product-recs">
  {{ 'pm-homepage.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'pm-product.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <div class="pm-product-recs-head">
    <h3 class="pm-serif">{{ section.settings.product_recommendations_heading }}</h3>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Shopify's dynamic ("related") recommendations need order/view
    history to have anything to suggest — a brand-new store, or a
    product with no sales yet, commonly gets zero back, which would
    otherwise leave this whole section blank forever. Falls back to a
    plain pull from Shop All (excluding the product being viewed)
    whenever that happens, so there's always something here — this
    quietly gets replaced by real recommendations once Shopify's
    engine actually has enough data to produce them, with no code
    change needed. related_collection is nil (not 0) when Shopify has
    nothing, and "nil == 0" is false in Liquid, so this has to check
    "unless > 0" rather than "== 0" to actually catch that case.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign display_products = related_collection.products -%}
  {%- unless related_collection.products_count > 0 -%}
    {%- assign display_products = collections.all.products -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Complementary products, set per-product in the Search & Discovery
    app (Admin > Apps > Search & Discovery > Recommendations), take
    priority over both Shopify's generic "related" engine and the
    Shop All fallback above -- a merchant's deliberate pairing beats
    an algorithm's guess or a plain grab-bag. Falls through to
    whichever of those two already applied when a product has none
    configured, so this is safe to ship before every product has
    complementary products set.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if complementary_products.size > 0 -%}
    {%- assign display_products = complementary_products -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if display_products.size > 0 -%}
    {%- assign rec_grid_id = 'pm-rec-grid-' | append: section.id -%}
    <div class="pm-scroll-row-wrap">
    <div class="pm-rec-grid" id="{{ rec_grid_id }}">
      {%- assign shown_count = 0 -%}
      {%- for rec_product in display_products -%}
        {%- if shown_count >= number_of_products -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if rec_product.id != product.id -%}
          {%- assign shown_count = shown_count | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Sibling color count (the "+5" in the reference). Most
            products here use a real Color variant (one product page,
            all colors within) -- for those, siblings are just this
            product's other color values. The title-prefix fallback
            below only matters for the rarer case where a color is
            still its own separate product (e.g. "Maxi Roma — Red").
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign rec_color_option = nil -%}
          {%- for option in rec_product.options_with_values -%}
            {%- assign option_name_downcase = option.name | downcase -%}
            {%- if option_name_downcase == 'color' or option_name_downcase == 'colour' -%}
              {%- assign rec_color_option = option -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- if rec_color_option -%}
            {%- assign sibling_count = rec_color_option.values.size | minus: 1 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Showcasing a different color per product (rather than
              always whatever sits first in variant position --
              usually the same color, e.g. White, on every product)
              so the row doesn't look monotonous. Cycles through this
              product's own color list using the tile's position in
              the row (forloop.index0 modulo how many colors this
              product has) instead of the `sample` filter -- plain
              array indexing, guaranteed to work everywhere. Variant
              images + alt text are already set up correctly per
              color in Admin, so this just has to find the variant
              for whichever color the index lands on and use its own
              image/price directly.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign rec_color_key = 'option' | append: rec_color_option.position -%}
            {%- assign rec_color_index = forloop.index0 | modulo: rec_color_option.values.size -%}
            {%- assign rec_color_value = rec_color_option.values[rec_color_index] -%}
            {%- assign rec_variant = rec_product.variants | where: rec_color_key, rec_color_value | first -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_image = rec_variant.featured_image | default: rec_product.featured_image -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_price = rec_variant.price | default: rec_product.price -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_price_prefix = '' -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_name = rec_product.title -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_color_name = rec_color_value -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_url = rec_product.url | append: '?variant=' | append: rec_variant.id -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Swatches for this product's other colors, shown on
              hover same as the Shop grid (pm-plp-swatches/pm-plp-
              swatch, reused as-is) -- encoded as
              name::css-color::url::image, joined with ';;'.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign rec_swatch_siblings = '' -%}
            {%- for other_value in rec_color_option.values -%}
              {%- unless other_value == rec_color_value -%}
                {%- assign other_rec_variant = rec_product.variants | where: rec_color_key, other_value | first -%}
                {%- assign rec_swatch_css = other_value | split: ' ' | last | handle -%}
                {%- capture rec_swatch_image -%}{% render 'pm-crystal-swatch-url', color_value: other_value %}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- assign rec_swatch_image = rec_swatch_image | strip -%}
                {%- if rec_swatch_image == blank and other_rec_variant.featured_image -%}
                  {%- assign rec_swatch_image = other_rec_variant.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- assign rec_sibling_entry = other_value | append: '::' | append: rec_swatch_css | append: '::' | append: rec_product.url | append: '?variant=' | append: other_rec_variant.id | append: '::' | append: rec_swatch_image -%}
                {%- assign rec_swatch_siblings = rec_swatch_siblings | append: rec_sibling_entry | append: ';;' -%}
              {%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- assign rec_swatch_list = rec_swatch_siblings | split: ';;' -%}
            {%- assign rec_swatch_visible = rec_swatch_list | slice: 0, 4 -%}
            {%- assign rec_swatch_overflow = rec_swatch_list.size | minus: rec_swatch_visible.size -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign rec_swatch_visible = '' | split: ';;' -%}
            {%- assign rec_swatch_overflow = 0 -%}
            {%- assign rec_base_title = rec_product.title | split: ' — ' | first -%}
            {%- assign sibling_count = 0 -%}
            {%- for sibling_product in collections.all.products -%}
              {%- if sibling_product.id != rec_product.id -%}
                {%- assign sibling_base = sibling_product.title | split: ' — ' | first -%}
                {%- if sibling_base == rec_base_title -%}
                  {%- assign sibling_count = sibling_count | plus: 1 -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_image = rec_product.featured_image -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_price = rec_product.price -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_price_prefix = '' -%}
            {%- if rec_product.price_varies -%}{%- assign rec_tile_price_prefix = 'From ' -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_name = rec_base_title -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_color_name = '' -%}
            {%- if rec_product.title contains ' — ' -%}
              {%- assign rec_tile_color_name = rec_product.title | split: ' — ' | last -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign rec_tile_url = rec_product.url -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Outer element is a plain div, not an <a>, so the swatch
            links below aren't nested inside another <a> -- browsers
            silently mangle nested anchors. Same pattern already used
            on the Shop grid (pm-plp-tile).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="pm-rec-tile pm-reveal" style="transition-delay: {{ forloop.index0 | times: 70 }}ms">
            <a href="{{ rec_tile_url }}" class="pm-rec-tile-link">
              <div class="pm-rec-tile-image">
                {%- if rec_tile_image -%}
                  <img src="{{ rec_tile_image | image_url: width: 800 }}" alt="{{ rec_tile_image.alt | escape | default: rec_tile_name }}" loading="lazy">
                {%- else -%}
                  {% render 'pm-media-placeholder', label: 'Photo', hover: true %}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <div class="pm-rec-tile-info">
                <div class="pm-rec-tile-row">
                  <span class="pm-rec-tile-name">{{ rec_tile_name }}{%- if rec_tile_color_name != blank %} <span class="pm-tile-color">{{ rec_tile_color_name }}</span>{%- endif -%}</span>
                  {%- if sibling_count > 0 -%}
                    <span class="pm-rec-tile-colors"><i></i>+{{ sibling_count }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
                <span class="pm-rec-tile-price">{{ rec_tile_price_prefix }}{{ rec_tile_price | money }}</span>
              </div>
            </a>
            {%- if rec_swatch_visible.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="pm-plp-swatches">
                {%- for entry in rec_swatch_visible -%}
                  {%- assign rec_swatch_parts = entry | split: '::' -%}
                  {%- assign rec_swatch_img = rec_swatch_parts[3] -%}
                  {%- assign rec_swatch_is_curated = false -%}
                  {%- if rec_swatch_img contains 'pm-swatch-' -%}{%- assign rec_swatch_is_curated = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                  <a href="{{ rec_swatch_parts[2] }}" class="pm-plp-swatch" style="background-color: {{ rec_swatch_parts[1] }};{% if rec_swatch_img != blank %} background-image: url({{ rec_swatch_img }});{% endif %}{% if rec_swatch_is_curated %} background-size: cover;{% endif %}" title="{{ rec_swatch_parts[0] | escape }}" aria-label="{{ rec_swatch_parts[0] | escape }}"></a>
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- if rec_swatch_overflow > 0 -%}
                  <span class="pm-plp-swatch-more">+{{ rec_swatch_overflow }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
    {% render 'pm-scroll-arrows', scroll_target: rec_grid_id %}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.product-recommendations.name",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.product-recommendations.settings.show_product_recommendations.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "product_recommendations_heading",
      "label": "t:sections.product-recommendations.settings.product_recommendations_heading.label",
      "default": "You may also like"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "related_count",
      "label": "t:sections.product-recommendations.settings.related_count.label",
      "default": 6,
      "min": 2,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1
    }
  ],
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["footer", "header", "custom.popups"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
